WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.420
Aktion T4.

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:02.693
Nazi Germany.

00:00:02.693 --> 00:00:05.159
1939 to 1945.

00:00:05.159 --> 00:00:06.750
Framed as mercy.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.647
Started with terminal illness.

00:00:08.647 --> 00:00:10.340
Expanded to disability.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.659
Then eliminated the program's critics.

00:00:12.659 --> 00:00:14.431
The pattern is documented.

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:15.965
The pattern is repeating.

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:16.784
Canada.

00:00:16.784 --> 00:00:17.556
MAID.

00:00:17.556 --> 00:00:19.636
2016 to present.

00:00:19.636 --> 00:00:21.204
Framed as compassion.

00:00:21.204 --> 00:00:23.147
Started with terminal illness.

00:00:23.147 --> 00:00:25.488
Expanded to non-terminal conditions.

00:00:25.488 --> 00:00:28.352
Mental illness approved for 2027.

00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:33.034
Both programs preceded by propaganda framing vulnerable populations as burdens.

00:00:33.034 --> 00:00:38.602
Both featured government cost-benefit analyses supporting the elimination of specific demographics.

00:00:38.602 --> 00:00:42.511
MAID deaths: one thousand and eighteen in 2016.

00:00:42.511 --> 00:00:46.636
Sixteen thousand, two hundred and sixty-seven in 2024.

00:00:46.636 --> 00:00:48.556
Fifteen hundred percent growth.

00:00:48.556 --> 00:00:50.715
The comparison is not rhetorical.

00:00:50.715 --> 00:00:52.932
The trajectory is mathematical.

00:00:52.932 --> 00:00:55.227
The government's own numbers make the case.
